{"id": "102", "question": "how to sync audiobook from iphone to itunes", "gt": "Based on the given passages, here's how to sync audiobooks from iPhone to iTunes:\n\n1. Connect your iPhone to your computer using a USB cable.\n2. Open iTunes on your computer.\n3. Click on the \"Audiobooks\" tab on the left side of the iTunes window.\n4. Check the boxes next to the audiobooks you want to sync to your iPhone.\n5. Click the \"Sync Audiobooks\" button and choose the audiobooks you want to transfer or select \"All Audiobooks\" to transfer all of them to your iPhone.\n6. Click \"Apply\" at the bottom of the screen to finish the syncing process.\n\nAlternatively, you can use Syncios Audiobook Transfer to transfer audiobooks from your computer to your iOS device. To do this, follow these steps:\n\n1. Launch Syncios Audiobook Transfer on your computer.\n2. Connect your iPhone to your computer using a USB cable.\n3. Click on the \"Books\" tab on the top menu bar.\n4. Select the audiobooks you want to transfer from your computer to your iPhone.\n5. Click the \"Import\" button to transfer the selected audiobooks to your iPhone.\n\nI hope this helps! Let me know if you have any further questions.", "pred": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_pd", "raw_output": "Answer: Unable to answer based on given passages.", "cot": "The reasoning steps are:\n\nUnable to answer based on given passages.\nI need to examine the given passages to determine if they contain any information about syncing an audiobook from an iPhone to iTunes. I'll look for specific details such as:\nExamine the given passages for any mention of:\n- An iPhone\n- iTunes\n- Audiobooks\n- Syncing process\n- Specific steps, tools, or methods related to transferring audiobooks between these items\n\nAnswer: Unable to answer based on given passages.", "time_sec": 86.158, "generation_time_seconds": 85.9759, "selection_time_seconds": 0.1818, "nemotron": {"method": "pd", "step_beam_size": 1, "num_rollout": 4, "num_foresight": 3, "cluster_num": 2, "sigma_rate": 1.0, "runtime": "transformers-trust-remote-code"}, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 4.14, "GAVIE-Rel": -1.0, "GAVIE-Acc": -1.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "103", "question": "how the body systems work together", "gt": "The various systems in the human body work together to ensure its normal functioning. For instance, the urinary system works with all other systems to clean the blood by removing waste products from the skeletal, muscular, digestive, respiratory, circulatory, and nervous systems. This includes organs like the kidneys and lower intestines. Similarly, the respiratory system also collaborates with all other systems to provide oxygen to all body parts and remove carbon dioxide from the muscular, digestive, skeletal, circulatory, urinary, and nervous systems. The respiratory system comprises the nose, larynx, trachea, and lungs.", "pred": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_pd", "raw_output": "Answer: Unable to answer based on given passages.", "cot": "The reasoning steps are:\n\nUnable to answer based on given passages.\nUnable to answer based on given passages.\nUnable to answer based on given passages.\n\nAnswer: Unable to answer based on given passages.", "time_sec": 55.412, "generation_time_seconds": 55.3818, "selection_time_seconds": 0.03, "nemotron": {"method": "pd", "step_beam_size": 1, "num_rollout": 4, "num_foresight": 3, "cluster_num": 2, "sigma_rate": 1.0, "runtime": "transformers-trust-remote-code"}, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 0, "GAVIE-Rel": -1.0, "GAVIE-Acc": -1.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "105", "question": "how the body systems work together", "gt": "Based on the provided passages, here's how the body systems work together:\n\n1. The skeletal, muscular, digestive, respiratory, circulatory, urinary, endocrine, lymphatic, immune, and nervous systems all work together to help keep the body functioning normally. (Passage 1)\n2. The urinary system works closely with all other systems of the body to clean blood from the body and remove waste products from the skeletal, muscular, digestive, respiratory, circulatory, and nervous systems. (Passage 2)\n3. The respiratory system provides oxygen for all body parts and removes carbon dioxide from the muscular, digestive, skeletal, circulatory, urinary, and nervous systems. (Passage 3)\n\nTherefore, the body systems work together in the following ways:\n\n* The skeletal system provides support and structure for the body, while the muscular system helps move the body and its parts.\n* The digestive system breaks down food into nutrients that can be absorbed and used by the body, while the respiratory system provides oxygen for energy production.\n* The circulatory system delivers oxygenated blood to the body's cells and removes carbon dioxide, while the urinary system removes waste products from the blood.\n* The endocrine system produces hormones that regulate various bodily functions, including growth and development, metabolism, and reproductive processes.\n* The lymphatic system helps defend the body against infection and disease, while the immune system fights off foreign invaders.\n* The nervous system controls and coordinates the body's functions, including movement, sensation, and thought processes.\n\nOverall, the body's systems work together in a complex interplay to maintain homeostasis and ensure the proper functioning of the body.", "pred": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_pd", "raw_output": "Answer: Unable to answer based on given passages.", "cot": "The reasoning steps are:\n\nUnable to answer based on given passages.\nAnswer: Unable to answer based on given passages.\nUnable to answer based on given passages.\n\nAnswer: Unable to answer based on given passages.", "time_sec": 68.566, "generation_time_seconds": 68.5343, "selection_time_seconds": 0.0313, "nemotron": {"method": "pd", "step_beam_size": 1, "num_rollout": 4, "num_foresight": 3, "cluster_num": 2, "sigma_rate": 1.0, "runtime": "transformers-trust-remote-code"}, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 2.11, "GAVIE-Rel": -1.0, "GAVIE-Acc": -1.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "106", "question": "how the body systems work together", "gt": "Based on the given passages, the body systems work together as follows:\n\nThe skeletal, muscular, digestive, respiratory, circulatory, urinary, endocrine, lymphatic, immune, and reproductive systems all work together to help keep the body functioning normally. The urinary system helps to clean waste products from the other systems, while the respiratory system provides oxygen for all body parts and removes carbon dioxide from the other systems. The nervous system plays a crucial role in coordinating the functions of all the other systems.", "pred": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_pd", "raw_output": "Answer: Unable to answer based on given passages.", "cot": "The reasoning steps are:\n\nI need the specific passages about how body systems work together to analyze the physical details step by step. Without the actual text passages containing information about bodily systems and their interactions, I cannot perform the required analysis of physical details, examples, numbers, or comparisons. Please provide the passages first so I can proceed with the step-by-step reasoning as instructed.\nUnable to answer based on given passages.\nUnable to answer based on given passages.\n\nAnswer: Unable to answer based on given passages.", "time_sec": 49.652, "generation_time_seconds": 49.6213, "selection_time_seconds": 0.0308, "nemotron": {"method": "pd", "step_beam_size": 1, "num_rollout": 4, "num_foresight": 3, "cluster_num": 2, "sigma_rate": 1.0, "runtime": "transformers-trust-remote-code"}, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 9.38, "GAVIE-Rel": -1.0, "GAVIE-Acc": -1.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "112", "question": "what is the difference between the leeward and windward islands?", "gt": "Based on the given passages, the main difference between the Windward Islands and the Leeward Islands is their exposure to the northeast trade winds (northeasterlies). The Windward Islands are exposed to the wind and are therefore wetter and receive more rainfall, while the Leeward Islands are away from the wind and are drier, but still receive some rainfall. Additionally, the Windward Islands are located southeast of the Caribbean Sea, while the Leeward Islands are located northwest of the Caribbean Sea.", "pred": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_pd", "raw_output": "Answer: Unable to answer based on given passages.", "cot": "The reasoning steps are:\n\nThe passages do not provide any information about the leeward and windward islands, so it is not possible to determine their differences based on the given text.\nThe passages do not contain any mention of the leeward and windward islands, their geographical locations, or any physical characteristics that would allow for a comparison of their differences. Since no relevant details are provided in the given text, it is not possible to determine their distinctions based on the available information.\nThe passages do not provide any information about the leeward and windward islands, their geographical locations, or any physical characteristics that would allow for a comparison of their differences. Since no relevant details are provided in the given text, it is not possible to determine their distinctions based on the available information.\n\nAnswer: Unable to answer based on given passages.", "time_sec": 99.761, "generation_time_seconds": 99.7276, "selection_time_seconds": 0.0331, "nemotron": {"method": "pd", "step_beam_size": 1, "num_rollout": 4, "num_foresight": 3, "cluster_num": 2, "sigma_rate": 1.0, "runtime": "